The owner of the item in the table is to coordinate (not necessarily do) the task. All three members will review deliverables and assist each other with connecting the various aspects of the system.
Testing will not be left for Phase 7. In Phase 6, each member will perform tests on functions being developed by her. The last week of testing will involve testing all the way through (workflows), connections, user acceptance, recommendations, fixes, and final demonstration.
Development of Phase 8 will also start before finishing Phase 7. For example, we could start developing the presentation/report structure, slide deck template, and demonstration plan before the system is completely ready. This is needed because both Phase 7 and 8 have the same deadline.
7.3 Resource Availability
The team has the primary resources needed for the prototype, including three personal laptops, internet access, a GitHub repository, programming tools, and free/low-cost database and AI services. No additional hardware resources are anticipated for the project during the semester.
The GitHub repository will contain the source code, issues, and contributors’ branch commits, representing each member’s project-specific contributions. Development will take place in individual branches, which will be merged after peer reviews.
Passwords, API tokens, and other private tokens will not be committed to the repository. They will be stored separately and installed in the project with tools that protect configuration data. The team might not be able to obtain actual records of the university’s assets, as such information might contain financial, legal, maintenance, and location details that the university administration might consider confidential. The prototype will be based on sample data, unless the university provides access to actual information.
The sample data should include records of various types, including assets, departments, users, requests, approvals, transfers, maintenance records, expenses, locations, and changes to assets’ locations and other attributes. It should be noted that such data will be fictional, and the university might ask to replace any realistic data with randomly-generated values.
The largest resource constraint is the expected learning curve of the technologies to be utilized in the project. The team’s project hours allocation includes 33 hours in the buffer zone for experiments with the technology. 

