7.5 Schedule and Resource Feasibility Decision
The remaining schedule is challenging but acheivble, given the proposed division of work and control of the project scope. Given the estimated number of hours required (129) versus the number of hours worked (162), there is a33-hour (20.4%) surplus.
The biggest schedule risk is the amount of work allocated for three members due to deliverables tied to testing and final-project submissions in the same week. The risk will be mitigated by starting the integration and some forms of testing during Week 6 instead of waiting till the final week.
The team will also prioritize essential asset, request, approval, transfer, maintenance, and reporting workflows before advanced AI functions. The latter will only be completed if the essential system is reliable and there is sufficient time.
With the given assumptions, I conclude that the schedule and resource availability are feasible with reservations. The project can proceed as proposed with weekly progress reviews, early start of testing, and no additional scope expansion beyond the requirements capture phase.
